{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794652958,"nonce":"otpW71xWPGp38kXJ991FdBey8nE=","title":"Review every CHECK constraint, and move the ones that may change out of CHECKs","message":"SQLite (so D1 and the user Durable Object) can't alter or drop a CHECK: ALTER TABLE only renames, adds or drops columns, and can't drop a column a table CHECK names. Changing one means rebuilding the table (create, copy, drop, rename, recreate indexes and triggers; defer_foreign_keys on D1), which reads and writes every row. card was already rebuilt once just to add the cloze kind (user migration 0004).\n\nReview each CHECK in api/migrations and api/src/user/migrations. Keep the ones that state invariants (start \u003e= 0, end \u003e start, json_valid, timestamp format, URL shape, 0/1 booleans). For lists and limits that may grow, use something that can change in a migration without a rebuild: a BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE trigger that RAISE(ABORT)s (drop and recreate it to change it), or a lookup table with a foreign key (as tag does), or validation in the API alone.\n\nCandidates found by grepping CHECK ... IN / BETWEEN:\n- D1 user_document.licence and the annotation licence list (a new licence)\n- D1 user_document.visibility (e.g. unlisted)\n- D1 user_document_annotation.kind and the per-kind data CHECK (a new kind; see the annotations bug)\n- D1 user_document.annotations_count BETWEEN 0 AND 2000 (raising MAX_ANNOTATIONS)\n- DO card.kind (recognition, production, cloze), word.status, reading_list.status, card.schedule_status (ts-fsrs's states), review.rating (FSRS's 1-4)\n- DO settings.new_per_day and new_forms_per_day BETWEEN 0 AND 1000\n\nConsider adding a CLAUDE.md note once decided: a CHECK is for what never changes.","files":null}]}